From 3faf55455db571fe0627fe804637f2f491b9d574 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 22:03:23 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] worker: the practice pool holds a connection for each job the
 worker runs at once, and each failed attempt logs its error's code (CAS-42.5
 on 3ac856d5)

CAS-42.5 on 3ac856d5 (run 41901463895) failed only because A price and C parse 4 completed on attempt 2. The worker runs
a job from each practice queue and four parses at once (fifteen), each holding one of the application login's
connections at a time, on a pool of four with a ten-second connection timeout: a month's price job and an audit report
hold theirs for minutes, so the concurrent phase's six jobs left two waiting, and on that slower runner past ten
seconds. The instrumented run 41913629020 (co-001/wip-sc1b-retry-1, harness only) showed it: A's second report and C's
parses 7 and 8 failed their first attempts with pg-pool's "timeout exceeded when trying to connect", raised in the
handler's transaction, while four longer jobs held the four connections. Production's worker task runs the same pool.

- practicePool (worker.ts; main.ts and the end-to-end worker) opens PRACTICE_JOB_SLOTS connections, counted from the
  queues' local concurrency (registry.ts: 15); the ten-second timeout stays (ADR 0055).
- Each failed attempt logs "job attempt failed" with the job's ID and type and attemptErrorCode's code
  (DB_POOL_TIMEOUT, DB_CONNECT_TIMEOUT, DB_<SQLSTATE>, a code the error carries, or its class), never its text.
- The weekly run prints those codes beside a job that completed on a later attempt (checks.ts attemptFailures); the
  check is unchanged.
- ADR 0083 records it ("The practice pool, 2026-11-04"); docs/runbooks/ci.md reads the codes.

Tests, each failing first: fifteen jobs at once each holding its transaction past a shortened timeout on the pool
main.ts opens (11 of 15 failed on four connections); the pool's size against startWorker's loops (4, now 15); each
failed attempt's line and code; the summary's codes beside a retried job.

